            "id": "8655149",
            "user": "BR",
            "timestamp": "10:24, 31 October 2012",
            "anon": false,
            "size": "(2,632 bytes)",
            "change": 2623,
            "summary": "(Reverted edits by 86.21.168.153 (Talk); changed back to last version by WikiHow Traduce)",
            "is_minor": true,
            "is_expert": false,
            "status": "reverted",
            "contribution_type": "revert",
            "reverted_by": "Zygomatt",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "[[Image:Labyrinthine circuit board lines 4.jpg|{{BASEPAGENAME}}|right|251px]]If you're looking for some helpful advice to make a working light bulb then you've come to the right place. Scroll down and let's get started!",
                    "[[Category:Electrical Maintenance]]",
                    "== Steps ==",
                    "=== Method 1 ===",
                    "#Get a 10-volt bulb, bulb holder, 9-volt battery and 2 wires. Using two wires of different colors makes this process easier.",
                    "#Screw a bulb into a bulb holder.",
                    "#Remove about an inch of wire covering from each end of the wires with a wire stripper or a pair of scissors.",
                    "#[[Image:Circuit Illustration.jpg|right|225px]]Connect one end of a wire to the positive end of a 1.5-volt battery and the other end to the center of the bulb holder. Generally, red is used to connect the positive end.",
                    "#Connect the other wire to the negative end of a 1.5-volt battery and the other end to the side of the bulb holder. Generally, black is used to connect the negative end.",
                    "#Now your bulb will light up!",
                    "=== Method 2 ===",
                    "#You can also use a power pack to make a circuit. To make a circuit in this way, You need to do the following:",
                    "#Place the power pack on the desk, ensuring that it is connected to the main supply.",
                    "#Collect all equipment needed, wires and bulbs, you do not need a battery for this circuit.",
                    "#Connect the circuit together, ensuring that there are know breaks in the circuit, (breaks mean that there is a gap in the circuit)",
                    "#Adjust the voltage by turning a dial on the power pack; this will give you varying degrees of light.",
                    "=== Optional Tweaks ===",
                    "#You can use a switch to turn the circuit on/off.  Instead of connecting the battery to the light bulb, connect the light bulb to the switch, then the switch to the battery.",
                    "",
                    "== Video ==",
                    "{{Video:Make a Circuit|}}",
                    "",
                    "== Tips ==",
                    "*Use one more battery for 3 volts power (bulb will light more brightly).",
                    "*Double check the wiring if you are having problems.",
                    "",
                    "== Warnings ==",
                    "*Don't use more than 3 volts or you might get shocked really hard.",
                    "",
                    "== Things You'll Need ==",
                    "*Light bulb",
                    "*Light bulb holder",
                    "*2 wires of different colors (copper works best)",
                    "*A 1.5-volt battery",
                    "*Battery holder (optional)",
                    "*Switch (optional)",
                    "",
                    "== Related wikiHows ==",
                    "*[[Install an Electrical Outlet from Scratch|How to Install an Electrical Outlet from Scratch]]",
                    "*[[Make a Voltage Divider Circuit|How to Make a Voltage Divider Circuit]]",
                    "*[[Do Common Electrical Repairs|How to Do Common Electrical Repairs]]",
                    "*[[Change a Stuck Lightbulb|How to Change a Stuck Lightbulb]]",
                    "*[[Make a Simple Electrical Circuit|How to Make a Simple Electrical Circuit]]",
                    "*[[Build a Parallel Circuit|How to Build a Parallel Circuit]]",
                    "[[es:hacer un circuito]]"
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "FUCK YOU!"
                ]
            }
        },
